broke under this war — a state not fighting it now faces a declared blockade because of it."},{"n":"Israel","id":"israel","dir":"both","w":"A direct participant in the exchange and the reason the leadership-strike tripwire stays armed; 51% of Israelis now read Trump and Netanyahu as driven by separate domestic interests."}],"escalation":{"rung":"Direct interstate strikes, leadership transition","dir":"volatile","phase":"Escalation with unresolved succession","up":["A strike on Iranian top leadership (tripwire NOT-TRIPPED but armed)","Khamenei succession produces a hardline consolidation","Houthi/Hormuz coupling drags in the wider Gulf","A miscalculation during the strike exchange"],"down":["Pakistan/Qatar/Oman mediation reviving the June MoU and Doha track","Hormuz reopening commercially reduces the economic stake","Both sides' demonstrated restraint at the very top of the target set","Exhaustion after nine days of costly exchanges"],"fw":["ladder","deterrence","security-dilemma"]},"macro":{"growth":"War-suppressed; sanctioned and interdicted","infl":"High","src":"Compiled reporting, 2026","note":"Exports move through the shadow fleet and settle through exchange houses and non-dollar channels after SWIFT exclusion — OFAC named Amin Exchange in May as a conduit for sanctioned banks, petrochemical exporters and the National Iranian Oil Company. CENTCOM reported stopping 27 ships to or from Iran by April. The measurable economy and the actual economy have diverged by design, which is what sanctions produce rather than what they prevent."},"inherit":{"name":"Operation Ajax and the Oil Concession","est":"1901-1953","status":"IN FORCE","what":"The 1901 D'Arcy concession gave a British subject exclusive rights to Persian oil for sixty years; the Anglo-Persian — later Anglo-Iranian — Oil Company kept books Iran was not permitted to audit and paid the British Treasury more in tax than it paid Iran in royalties. When <b>Mohammad Mossadegh nationalised the company in 1951</b> after parliament voted unanimously for it, Britain blockaded Iranian oil exports and, with the CIA, organised the <b>August 1953 coup</b> that removed him and restored the Shah with expanded powers. The CIA acknowledged its role in 2013.","now":"<b>The question Mossadegh asked — who decides what Iran's resources are for — is being answered by ordnance for the fourth time in seventy years.</b> The 1953 coup is the founding grievance of Iranian anti-Americanism, the reason 1979 took the form it did, and the reference point every Iranian government invokes. <b>Stated US justifications for the 2026 war have included 'taking Iran's oil and gas resources'</b> — which places the current campaign in the same category as the original dispute rather than a separate one.","change":"Nothing structural. <b>The war began 28 February 2026 and killed Khamenei in its opening strike; five months on, Trump states the strategy is to keep hitting until Tehran cannot take it.</b> Mediation runs through Qatar, Oman and Pakistan because no Western state is trusted by both parties."}},{"id":"lebanon","cat":"military","region":"Middle East","subregion":"Middle East","name":"Lebanon — Framework Signed (Contested)","sub":"Trilateral framework signed · Hezbollah 'null & void'","domain":"Framework → Disputed Implementation","sev":"high","status":"volatile","since":"Jun 22 2026","esc":78,"lat":33.3,"lon":35.4,"trend":"up","w14":false,"diplomacy_active":true,"esc_history":[76,76,76,75,75,75,75,75,75,78],"cas":"IDF Cpt. Hazutt killed; hundreds since Apr 17","disp":"1M+ displaced (>20% of Lebanon)","flag":"🇱🇧","note":"22-24 JUL 2026 — DIRECT TALKS IN ROME, AND AN ANNEXATION CLAIM DENIED: the SIXTH ROUND of Israel-Lebanon peace talks opened at the US EMBASSY IN ROME — and it is the FIRST DAY OF DIRECT NEGOTIATIONS, a format change after five indirect rounds · NETANYAHU claimed some CHRISTIAN-MAJORITY VILLAGES in southern Lebanon had ASKED TO BE ANNEXED by Israel for protection from Hezbollah; villages in the MARJAYOUN DISTRICT PUBLICLY DENIED seeking annexation — the denial is the story, and it is the sectarian-fragmentation playbook this platform tracks from Syria's Sweida to Gaza's clan militias · the Israeli Commando Brigade struck Hezbollah operatives near NABATIEH; UNIFIL continues to report ceasefire violations · 57,000+ PEOPLE REMAIN IN 516 COLLECTIVE SHELTERS, hesitant to return · CORRECTION + UPDATE — THE 2026 LEBANON WAR: this file previously framed Lebanon primarily through the 2024 Israel-Hezbollah war. A SECOND war was fought in 2026: escalation from March amid the Iran war, Israeli airstrikes and ground operations across Lebanon against Hezbollah rocket and drone fire, with MORE THAN 2,000 KILLED AND OVER 1 MILLION DISPLACED by mid-April · a US-brokered 10-day truce took effect 16-17 Apr 2026, and Israel-Lebanon PEACE TALKS opened during 2026 (the Rome round this file logged is part of that track) · STRUCTURAL POINT: the Iran-war ceasefire arrangements did NOT formally include Lebanon — that exclusion is why hostilities continued here after the wider truce, and why the Lebanese file is negotiated separately · Israel still occupies positions on the Lebanese side of the border; the disarmament deadline has slipped from end-2025, and the monitoring committee (Lebanon, Israel, France, US, UN) continues to convene · JUL 14-15 — ROME TALKS: Israeli and Lebanese officials in a new round of US-mediated talks in Rome (two days), following the June preliminary agreement to end the fighting · Trump told Netanyahu directly to start REDEPLOYING out of Lebanon (and Syria) — patron pressure now points toward de-escalation on this front · Trilateral framework SIGNED Jun 26 — IDF withdraws from 2 pilot zones, LAF oversees disarmament · Hezbollah (Qassem): 'null & void' · Katz: not 'a millimeter' more · Haaretz: 'Gaza Strip 2' · permanent-deal odds 1.4% · Israeli drone strikes/artillery continued across the south (Nabatieh al-Fawqa, Bint Jbeil) despite framework; relief volunteers under fire · US told Iran at Doha it would \"restrain Israel\"; pilot-zone withdrawal framed as \"first step\" · Israeli strikes continued across south post-framework; permanent-deal odds remain low; US \"restrain Israel\" pledge untested","leverage":[{"actor":"Israel","asset":"Occupation of S.Lebanon zone; pilot-zone withdrawal as chip","str":"hi"},{"actor":"United States","asset":"Mediation; ties Lebanon to Iran track","str":"hi"},{"actor":"Hezbollah","asset":"Spoiler veto — rejected framework as 'null & void'","str":"md"},{"actor":"Lebanese Armed Forces","asset":"To receive pilot zones + oversee disarmament (untested)","str":"md"}],"gov":[{"src":"US State Dept (Rubio)","detail":"Announced framework as 'beginning of the beginning'"},{"src":"Israel (Katz)","detail":"'No territorial ambitions' but won't withdraw 'a millimeter' beyond pilot zones"},{"src":"Lebanese government","detail":"Signed; declared Hezbollah 'enemy of Lebanon'"}],"mil":"The trilateral framework was signed June 26 in Washington: IDF withdraws from two pilot zones, the LAF takes over and oversees Hezbollah disarmament. But violence continued — Hezbollah killed IDF Cpt. Hazutt, and a car-bomb attempt struck Holon inside Israel.","pol":"Katz won't withdraw 'a millimeter' beyond the pilot zones until Hezbollah disarms; Qassem calls the framework 'null and void,' a 'surrender.' Haaretz warns of a 'Gaza Strip 2'; permanent-deal odds fell to 1.4%.","eco":"Weak energy-market transmission; over 1M displaced (>20% of Lebanon).","assess":"Lebanon holds at 76 — it rose because the framework got signed, but of its three negotiation strands one is signed, one collapsed (disarmament), and one stalled. The signed paper may institutionalize an indefinite Israeli presence rather than resolve anything.","tclass":"conflict","tier":"SEVERE","hist_real":true,"as_of":"1 Aug 2026","tracked_since":"Wk4 (2026)","domain_tag":"Military","external":[{"actor":"🇮🇷 Iran","side":"Hezbollah","flow":"Historic funder/armer; supply lines degraded after Syria's fall + the 2026 war","tier":"documented","for":"Forward deterrence; the Axis of Resistance's last major arm"},{"actor":"🇮🇱 Israel","side":"belligerent","flow":"Continues strikes; demands Hezbollah disarmament as the framework's core","tier":"documented","for":"Eliminate the northern threat"},{"actor":"🇺🇸🇫🇷 US/France","side":"Lebanese state","flow":"Back the framework + the LAF as the sole armed authority; financial conditionality","tier":"documented","for":"Rebuild a state monopoly on force; break Iranian influence"}],"contested":{"summary":"The fight over who won, who must disarm, and whose money rebuilds — every number is a weapon.","claims":[{"claim":"Hezbollah won a 'divine victory' by surviving; disarmament is off the table and reconstruction is its to lead.","who":"Hezbollah — the survival-as-victory frame that preserves its armed status and social legitimacy.","evid":"Command decimated, arsenal degraded, Iranian resupply constricted, community surveys show declining confidence in its reconstruction capacity — but it retains weapons and the state cannot compel disarmament. Both 'defeated' and 'undefeated' are simultaneously arguable, which is the problem.","status":"CONTESTED — victory narrative vs degraded reality"},{"claim":"Gulf/IMF reconstruction conditionality is Western blackmail against the resistance.","who":"Hezbollah-aligned media — reframing donor conditions as aggression.","evid":"The ~$7B GCC pledges and IMF program are explicitly conditioned on disarmament and banking reform — that's documented leverage, not hidden. Calling it blackmail is the counter-frame that makes accepting it betrayal.","status":"DOCUMENTED conditionality, CONTESTED meaning"}]},"econlev":[{"holder":"Gulf states (Saudi + UAE)","channel":"Conditional reconstruction pledges","exp":"HIGH","detail":"~$7B in combined GCC pledges — Saudi ~$5B tied explicitly to Hezbollah disarmament, UAE ~$2B tied to banking reform. Both conditional, both unmet as of 2026. The money is the lever: it flows only if the state, not Hezbollah, controls the south."},{"holder":"IMF / World Bank","channel":"Program + bridge financing","exp":"HIGH","detail":"IMF disbursements blocked pending parliamentary action on the banking-restructuring, BdL-governance and depositor-protection laws. ~$14B war damage, $11B+ reconstruction need, Eurobonds at 6-10 cents on the dollar since the 2020 default — no restructuring without an IMF deal first."},{"holder":"Hezbollah / Iran","channel":"Parallel patronage (declining)","exp":"MED","detail":"Hezbollah historically funded post-war reconstruction directly (2006 model). Community surveys now show declining confidence in its ability to repeat that — the war weakened both the group and its Iranian financing, opening space for the state to reclaim legitimacy."},{"holder":"Diaspora remittances","channel":"Rentier lifeline","exp":"MED","detail":"Lebanon's independence-era model relies on diaspora remittances and Gulf inflows over domestic industry — a rentier structure that makes it acutely vulnerable to external shocks and to the political mood of Gulf donors."}],"history":{"roots":"Lebanon's fragility is built into its founding bargain. Independence (1943) came with a sectarian power-sharing system dividing power among Maronite Christians, Sunnis, and Shias — a formula that calcified into gridlock and warlord fiefdoms. A 15-year civil war (1975-90) devastated the country; Syria and Israel occupied parts of it. Out of the war and Israel's occupation of the south rose Hezbollah — a Shia militia-cum-party, armed by Iran, stronger than the national army. Its wars with Israel, the 2019 financial collapse (one of the worst in modern history), and the 2020 Beirut blast hollowed the state. The 2024 war badly weakened Hezbollah, opening a fraught chance to rebuild state authority. The roots: sectarian power-sharing, a state weaker than its militias, and a rentier economy dependent on outside money.","timeline":[{"date":"1943","e":"Independence with a sectarian power-sharing system."},{"date":"1975-90","e":"Civil war devastates Lebanon."},{"date":"1982","e":"Israel invades; Hezbollah forms in resistance, backed by Iran."},{"date":"2005","e":"PM Hariri assassinated; Syria forced to withdraw."},{"date":"2006","e":"Hezbollah-Israel war."},{"date":"2019","e":"Financial system collapses; savings wiped out."},{"date":"2020","e":"Beirut port explosion devastates the capital."},{"date":"2024","e":"Israel-Hezbollah war badly degrades Hezbollah."},{"date":"2025-26","e":"Reconstruction and disarmament tied to conditional Gulf/IMF money."},{"date":"Mar-Apr 2026","e":"Second Israel-Hezbollah war amid the Iran conflict: 2,000+ killed, 1M+ displaced; US-brokered 10-day truce takes effect 16 April; Israel-Lebanon peace talks open."}],"actors":[{"name":"Hezbollah","bio":"Iran-backed Shia party and militia, long stronger than the state; weakened by the 2024 war, resisting disarmament."},{"name":"Lebanese state","bio":"A weak, sectarian government trying to reclaim authority and unlock frozen Gulf/IMF reconstruction funds."},{"name":"Iran","bio":"Hezbollah's patron; its regional setbacks reduce the flow that once made Hezbollah dominant."},{"name":"Gulf states / IMF","bio":"Hold the reconstruction purse strings — conditioned explicitly on Hezbollah's disarmament and banking reform."}],"bridge":"The reconstruction-for-disarmament standoff is the founding bargain renegotiated at gunpoint: Traboulsi's history shows every Lebanese settlement (1943, Taif) has been a sectarian shareholders' agreement underwritten by outside money — and the ~$7B Gulf conditionality is simply the new term sheet, with Hezbollah's arsenal as the contested collateral. The Rome talks and Trump's redeploy push could close the southern front; nothing on the table yet touches the deeper structure — a state whose every rebuilding has been financed by patrons who thereby own a faction. · AND NOW, JUL 2026: 2,000+ dead and a million displaced from the 2026 war, with the disarmament question unresolved. The confessional formula the French mandate fixed in 1943 still allocates power — and still cannot produce a state monopoly on force.","sources":[{"work":"A History of Modern Lebanon","author":"Fawwaz Traboulsi","year":"2007 (2nd ed. 2012)","note":"The Lebanese-authored standard — sectarianism as political economy, not ancient hatred."},{"work":"Hezbollah: The Global Footprint of Lebanon's Party of God","author":"Matthew Levitt / balanced against Amal Saad, 'Hizbullah: Politics and Religion'","year":"2013 / 2002","note":"Paired readings — the security-state view and the movement's own social logic."},{"work":"World Bank Lebanon Economic Monitors","author":"World Bank","year":"2019-26","note":"Primary record of the financial collapse — 'among the world's worst since the 1850s.'"}]},"human":{"dead":6000,"disp":1000000,"famine":false,"aid":"reconstruction-gated","note":"Two wars in three years: the 2024 Israel-Hezbollah war (~4,000 killed) and the 2026 Lebanon war (2,000+ killed, 1M+ displaced by mid-April before the 16 Apr truce). Return is blocked by rubble, unexploded ordnance, and the unresolved disarmament standoff that gates reconstruction money.","est":true,"basis":"Order-of-magnitude working figure — no single authoritative running count exists for this theater"},"rival":{"conf":"HIGH","lens":"A sectarian shareholders' state where every rebuilding is financed by patrons who thereby own a faction.","alt":"A straightforward Iran-proxy reading centers Hezbollah as Tehran's forward arm above the domestic political-economy frame.","why":"The proxy dimension is real but incomplete — it can't explain the reconstruction-conditionality politics or the sectarian-finance structure that predates Hezbollah. HIGH on the political-economy frame."},"refs":[{"t":"UN OCHA · Lebanon displacement","u":"https://www.unocha.org/lebanon"},{"t":"Ceasefire-violation reporting, disarmament track","u":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/israel-kills-least-5-people-082918514.html"},{"t":"World Bank Lebanon Economic Monitor","u":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/lebanon"},{"t":"Crisis Group: Lebanon","u":"https://www.crisisgroup.org/middle-east-north-africa/east-mediterranean-mena/lebanon"}],"checkmode":"CHECKED","escwhy":"78 = post-2026-war reconstruction under an unresolved disarmament question, with 2,000+ killed and 1M+ displaced in the recent fighting.","log":[{"v":"v59","d":"21 Jul 2026","c":"Provenance, check-mode and escalation-derivation fields added; no substantive content change this cycle."}],"spill":[{"n":"Israel","dir":"both","w":"Sixth round of talks, now DIRECT, at the US embassy in Rome; simultaneously the Commando Brigade strikes Hezbollah near Nabatieh and forces entered Quneitra-adjacent villages. Talking and striking at once.","id":"israel"},{"n":"Syria","dir":"in","w":"Damascus now INTERDICTS Iranian weapons bound for Hezbollah — the supply line that sustained the group is being cut by its former guarantor's successor.","id":"syria"},{"n":"Iran","dir":"in","w":"Hezbollah's degradation and the disarmament question are downstream of the Iran war; the patron is weakened and the proxy exposed.","id":"iran-us"},{"n":"Israel (annexation claim)","dir":"both","w":"Netanyahu claimed southern Christian villages sought annexation; Marjayoun District publicly denied it — the sectarian-fragmentation playbook, and the denial is the story.","id":"israel"},{"n":"Gaza","id":"gaza","dir":"both","w":"The same 'day after' problem in two theatres: Hamas refusing decommissioning under Resolution 2803 mirrors the Hezbollah disarmament question being negotiated in Rome. Each outcome sets a precedent for the other."},{"n":"West Bank","id":"west-bank","dir":"in","w":"The same sectarian-fragmentation template — Netanyahu’s claim that southern Christian villages sought annexation, which Marjayoun denied, applied across a different border."}],"escalation":{"rung":