 Peace; Netanyahu: no reconstruction until Hamas disarmed + Gaza demilitarized (the unresolved crux)","leverage":[{"actor":"Israel","asset":"'Unlimited' Gaza security-zone control; Yellow Line enforcement","str":"hi"},{"actor":"Hamas","asset":"Refusal to disarm; rejected Mladenov plan; residual hostage/body leverage","str":"md"},{"actor":"Board of Peace / Gulf","asset":"$5B+ reconstruction capital (competing with Iran $300B)","str":"md"}],"gov":[{"src":"UNRWA","detail":"73,000+ Palestinian deaths (mid-2026)"},{"src":"Board of Peace (Mladenov)","detail":"Gaza demilitarization plan apparently rejected by Hamas"}],"mil":"Gaza continues to smolder under a shaky ceasefire. The Jerusalem Post notes Israel is 'running out of quality targets' — now hitting low-level operatives rather than senior figures. IDF strikes on Khan Younis tent camps killed two June 29.","pol":"The Board of Peace's demilitarization plan, presented by Nickolay Mladenov, was apparently rejected by Hamas. The Gulf-capital competition with Iran's $300B reconstruction persists.","eco":"Reconstruction pledged ($5B+) but not flowing; Gulf capital is being pulled toward Iran's larger $300B ask.","assess":"Gaza holds at 77. The July 6 move is significant diplomatically if not on the ground: Hamas dissolved its government to hand governance to the technocratic NCAG — but pointedly omitted disarmament, the phase-two crux — putting symbolic pressure back on Israel while changing nothing about who controls the streets. Phase two has 'launched' (last hostage body returned, Board of Peace meeting in Cyprus), yet the NCAG remains stuck in Cairo, the international stabilization force hasn't materialized, Israel is seizing ~70% of the Strip, and the toll keeps climbing (73,074+; roughly one child a day since the ceasefire). A June UN commission found ongoing genocide. The war's kinetic phase is largely spent; the political phase is deadlocked on disarmament.","diplomacy":[{"name":"Gaza peace plan phase two","desc":"Launched after last hostage body returned; full demilitarization + reconstruction + NCAG governance — but no timeline set, int'l force not deployed","status":"active","next":"NCAG handover conditions unset"},{"name":"Hamas government dissolution","desc":"Jul 6: Hamas dissolved its Gaza govt to hand to technocratic committee — but omitted disarmament (the phase-two crux); analysts call it a savvy pressure move on Israel","status":"active","next":"Israel response / NCAG entry"},{"name":"Hamas disarmament","desc":"Still refused; Israel says it will restart fighting to 'complete the mission' if Hamas won't disarm","status":"stalled","next":"the central deadlock"}],"tclass":"conflict","tier":"SEVERE","hist_real":true,"as_of":"1 Aug 2026","tracked_since":"Wk4 (2026)","domain_tag":"Military","external":[{"actor":"🇺🇸 US","side":"Israel / Board of Peace","flow":"Architect of the Board of Peace framework; funds and arms Israel; oversees the NCAG transition","tier":"documented","for":"Regional order; the Abraham-Accords normalization track"},{"actor":"🇶🇦🇪🇬🇹🇷 Qatar/Egypt/Turkey","side":"mediators / Hamas channel","flow":"Brokered the ceasefire and the Hamas dissolution; Egypt controls Rafah; Qatar hosts the political bureau","tier":"documented","for":"Regional standing; prevent a Gaza spillover"},{"actor":"🇮🇷 Iran","side":"Hamas/PIJ (degraded)","flow":"Historic patron of the Axis of Resistance; severely degraded after the 2026 war","tier":"documented","for":"Forward deterrence against Israel — now largely dismantled"}],"econlev":[{"holder":"Israel","channel":"Crossings + reconstruction","exp":"HIGH","detail":"Controls all cargo crossings; Netanyahu ties reconstruction to Hamas disarmament + demilitarization — aid as leverage over the political outcome"}],"contested":{"summary":"A ceasefire whose central term neither side agrees on.","claims":[{"claim":"Netanyahu ties reconstruction to Hamas disarmament and demilitarization.","who":"Israel — conditioning aid preserves leverage over the political outcome indefinitely.","evid":"Hamas's dissolution of its Gaza government is formalized (handed to the NCAG under the Board of Peace). Disarmament is not agreed. Reconstruction is therefore hostage to an unresolved condition.","status":"CONTESTED — the crux is deliberately unresolved"}]},"history":{"roots":"The Gaza war is the most violent chapter of a conflict as old as the state of Israel. Gaza — a tiny, densely populated strip — filled with Palestinian refugees expelled or fleeing during Israel's 1948 founding (the Nakba). Israel occupied it in 1967, withdrew settlers in 2005, and imposed a blockade after Hamas — an Islamist movement committed to armed resistance — won elections and seized the strip in 2007. Successive wars followed. Hamas's Oct 7 2023 attack, the deadliest day for Jews since the Holocaust, triggered an Israeli campaign of unprecedented destruction. The root is the unresolved question of Palestinian statehood and self-determination, and two peoples' claims to the same land.","timeline":[{"date":"1948","e":"Israel's founding; the Nakba displaces ~700,000 Palestinians, many into Gaza."},{"date":"1967","e":"Israel occupies Gaza in the Six-Day War."},{"date":"2005","e":"Israel withdraws settlers and soldiers from Gaza."},{"date":"2007","e":"Hamas seizes Gaza; Israel and Egypt impose a blockade."},{"date":"2008-21","e":"Repeated Israel-Hamas wars."},{"date":"7 Oct 2023","e":"Hamas attack kills ~1,200 in Israel; ~250 taken hostage."},{"date":"2023-24","e":"Israel's campaign devastates Gaza; tens of thousands killed."},{"date":"2025","e":"A fragile ceasefire and hostage-exchange framework is implemented."},{"date":"2026","e":"Truce holds unevenly; hundreds reported killed since signing; reconstruction and governance unresolved."}],"actors":[{"name":"Hamas","bio":"Islamist movement governing Gaza since 2007; launched the Oct 7 attack. Weakened militarily but not eliminated; the governance question after it is unresolved."},{"name":"Israel","bio":"Seeks the destruction of Hamas and return of hostages; faces international legal scrutiny (an ICJ case) over the campaign's conduct."},{"name":"United States","bio":"Israel's chief backer and the broker of the ceasefire framework and the 'Board of Peace' transition plan."},{"name":"Egypt / Qatar","bio":"Mediators and would-be trainers of a post-Hamas Gaza police force; Egypt controls the Rafah crossing."}],"bridge":"The current 'day after' fight is the hundred-year question in miniature: every proposed administrator of Gaza (the Board of Peace, Egyptian-trained police, a reformed PA) is an answer to who rules Palestinians other than Palestinians — the arrangement Khalidi's century of declarations, mandates, and accords has always produced. The Knesset's attorney-general law and the Netanyahu-as-obstacle briefings show the occupier's own institutions buckling under the war's weight; the ICJ case and the US anti-ICC campaign show the legal order itself becoming a front. The ceasefire holds bodies apart; nothing yet has touched the question. · AND NOW, JUL 2026: Resolution 2803 has created a Board of Peace and a stabilisation force to supervise a disarmament Hamas refuses. The 1947 partition's unfinished question — who governs, under whose authority — is being asked again with the same absence of an answer.","sources":[{"work":"The Hundred Years' War on Palestine","author":"Rashid Khalidi","year":"2020","note":"The Palestinian-authored framework — a century of externally imposed settlements, 1917 to the present."},{"work":"The Question of Palestine","author":"Edward W. Said","year":"1979","note":"The foundational text on Palestine as seen versus Palestine as lived."},{"work":"The Ethnic Cleansing of Palestine","author":"Ilan Pappé","year":"2006","note":"The 1948 expulsions from the Israeli 'new historians' archive."},{"work":"UN OCHA / ICJ provisional-measures orders","author":"UN / ICJ","year":"2024-26","note":"Primary casualty documentation and the live legal record."}]},"human":{"dead":71386,"disp":1900000,"famine":true,"aid":"throttled at crossings","note":"Gaza health ministry toll: 71,386 killed, at least 420 of them since the Oct-2025 ceasefire began. Most of the 2.2M population displaced; aid access restricted despite the truce, with Israel blocking supplies and banning several international organisations. Resolution 2803's Board of Peace reports improvements; the UN reports needs 'remain immense'.","est":false,"basis":"Gaza MoH / UN OCHA running toll"},"rival":{"conf":"MOD","lens":"The unresolved question of Palestinian self-determination; every 'day after' plan reproduces rule-of-Palestinians-by-others.","alt":"A security-first reading centers Hamas's Oct 7 attack and hostage-taking as the proximate driver that any state would answer militarily — structure explains the century, not the specific war's conduct.","why":"The platform holds the structural frame for the conflict and the security frame for the trigger; contest over the campaign's proportionality is logged in Contested, not resolved here. MOD."},"refs":[{"t":"Times of Israel · Board of Peace on disarmament timing (1 Aug 2026)","u":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog-august-01-2026/"},{"t":"CNN · phase-two requirements (31 Jul 2026)","u":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/07/31/world/live-news/iran-war-trump"},{"t":"Times of Israel · liveblog (31 Jul 2026)","u":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog-july-31-2026/"},{"t":"UN Security Council Report · Middle East monthly forecast (Jul 2026)","u":"https://www.securitycouncilreport.org/monthly-forecast/2026-07/the-middle-east-including-the-palestinian-question-25.php"},{"t":"ACLED · Middle East Overview July 2026","u":"https://acleddata.com/update/middle-east-overview-july-2026"},{"t":"Just Security · Early Edition (31 Jul 2026)","u":"https://www.justsecurity.org/150786/early-edition-july-31-2026/"},{"t":"NPR · world (30-31 Jul 2026)","u":"https://www.npr.org/sections/world/"}],"checkmode":"SWEPT","escwhy":"77