ld Bank reclassified the PHILIPPINES as upper-middle-income · JUL 20 — $4 GASOLINE RETURNS: US average pump prices are back to ~$4.00/gallon as strikes and counterstrikes continue; Wall Street steadied as AI stocks recovered part of last week's sharp losses. The war's cost has reached the American consumer directly — the transmission channel that historically ends wars faster than casualty figures do · JUL 2026 — THE CHOKEPOINT REACHES THE REAL ECONOMY: Hormuz disruption has produced FUEL SHORTAGES IN PARTS OF ASIA with rippling effects across global supply chains — the transmission the platform's chokepoint thesis predicts, now observable rather than modelled · with ~25% of seaborne oil and ~20% of LNG normally transiting the strait, the war premium is no longer a market abstraction but a physical scarcity in importing states · JUL 15-17 — CHINA'S AI-EXPORT QUARTER: GDP boosted by strong exports 'thanks partly to the boom in artificial intelligence' while consumer spending and business investment lag — the export-led AI economy compensating for domestic softness · global perception surveys shift TOWARD China and away from the US (post Trump-Xi Beijing summit) — the soft-power ledger moving with the hard-power one · Oil 'relatively contained' through exchange (Swissquote) — reserve releases + oversupply · $6B Iran assets unfrozen · Kenya/Comoros fuel protests · shipping normalization slowed not reversed","leverage":[{"actor":"Iran","asset":"Hormuz control — can spike oil, but impact contained this round","str":"hi"},{"actor":"Strategic reserves/OPEC+","asset":"Releases cushioned the shock","str":"md"},{"actor":"Shipping industry","asset":"Risk-pricing — normalization slowed","str":"md"}],"gov":[{"src":"IMF","detail":"Pre-war growth track (3.3%) holding through the stress test"},{"src":"Qatar","detail":"Released $6B in frozen Iranian assets"}],"mil":"N/A — but the exchange was the first real stress test of the recovery, and it largely held.","pol":"Swissquote: oil im