onal and then global one. The 2011 Arab Spring ousted long-ruling Saleh; the transition failed, and in 2014 the Houthis — a Zaidi-Shia revivalist movement from the north — seized the capital Sanaa. A Saudi-led coalition intervened in 2015 to restore the government, producing the world's worst humanitarian crisis. Iran armed the Houthis, turning Yemen into a Saudi-Iranian proxy theater. After 2023 the Houthis globalized the war by attacking Red Sea shipping in solidarity with Gaza, drawing US and UK strikes. The roots: a north-south divide, Zaidi marginalization, and Yemen's position astride the Bab-el-Mandeb chokepoint.","timeline":[{"date":"1990","e":"North and South Yemen unify under Saleh."},{"date":"2011","e":"Arab Spring uprising ousts Saleh."},{"date":"2014","e":"Houthis seize Sanaa."},{"date":"2015","e":"Saudi-led coalition intervenes; humanitarian catastrophe begins."},{"date":"2022","e":"A UN truce sharply reduces frontline fighting."},{"date":"2023","e":"Houthis begin Red Sea shipping attacks over Gaza."},{"date":"2024-25","e":"US/UK airstrikes on the Houthis; shipping reroutes around Africa."},{"date":"2026","e":"Houthis entrenched as the dominant Yemeni power and a Red Sea veto-holder."},{"date":"2 Dec 2025","e":"STC launches a large offensive across southern Yemen, seizing Hadhramaut and announcing plans for an independence referendum."},{"date":"7-9 Jan 2026","e":"Saudi-backed government forces retake Hadhramaut and enter Aden; al-Zoubaidi is expelled from the PLC, charged with treason and flees to the UAE. The STC ANNOUNCES ITS DISSOLUTION."},{"date":"Jan 2026","e":"The UAE withdraws its remaining forces from Yemen — the patron folds the project."},{"date":"28 Mar 2026","e":"Houthis fire missiles at southern Israel, their first strike since the US-Israel war with Iran began."},{"date":"Jul 2026","e":"Houthis break the four-year Saudi truce, striking Abha airport."}],"actors":[{"name":"Houthis (Ansar Allah)","bio":"Zaidi-Shia movement controlling north