e imagery shows reconstruction at al-Jufra air base through Apr 2026 — Moscow is building the North Africa foothold that supplies the Sahel Africa Corps deployments (Mali, Burkina, Niger) · CONTRADICTION: Moscow has shifted most Sudan support from the RSF to the SAF — but its forces in Libya do not interfere with Haftar's arms flow to the RSF (Jamestown) · Libya remains split: Tripoli (GNU, UN-recognized) vs Tobruk/Benghazi (Haftar/LNA); elections perpetually deferred · al-Wigh, Maaten al-Sarra, Brak al-Shati, al-Khadim, al-Jufra = the airbase network","leverage":[{"actor":"Haftar / LNA","asset":"Controls southeastern Libya incl. al-Kufra — the northern gate of the RSF pipeline; rents territory to the UAE and Russia simultaneously","str":"hi"},{"actor":"Russia (Africa Corps)","asset":"Tobruk basing agreement + al-Jufra reconstruction — the logistics bridge from the Mediterranean to the Sahel deployments","str":"hi"},{"actor":"UAE","asset":"Runs the northern arms route through Libyan airspace and airfields; Haftar's principal financier","str":"hi"},{"actor":"Egypt","asset":"Diplomatic pressure that briefly CLOSED al-Kufra (Jan 2026) — proof the corridor can be shut, and that no one has sustained the effort","str":"md"},{"actor":"GNU (Tripoli)","asset":"UN recognition and the west — but no control over the south, where the corridor runs","str":"lo"}],"gov":[{"src":"ISW / Critical Threats (Jan 2026)","detail":"Documents the two UAE air routes to the RSF (northern via Libya, southern via Chad); eastern Libyan authorities closed al-Kufra Airport Jan 19 2026 under Egyptian pressure"},{"src":"NGA/Tearline OSINT (Jun 2026)","detail":"Satellite imagery: Russia developing air-base infrastructure (al-Jufra hangar reconstruction through Apr 2026) to secure a North Africa and Sahel foothold; Feb 2025 Haftar-Russia-Belarus tripartite agreement on Tobruk"},{"src":"Jamestown Foundation","detail":"Moscow shifted most Sudan backing to the SAF, yet its forces in Libya do not interfere with Haftar's arms supply to the RSF"},{"src":"UN Panel of Experts / CNN flight-tracking","detail":"IL-76 and AN-26 cargo flights from Kufra to RSF-controlled Sudan documented repeatedly since 2023"}],"econlev":[{"holder":"Haftar / LNA","channel":"Territorial rent + oil","exp":"HIGH","detail":"Sells transit rights to the UAE and basing to Russia; the LNA also controls much of Libya's oil crescent — leverage over a state whose entire economy is hydrocarbons"},{"holder":"Russia","channel":"Basing-for-influence","exp":"HIGH","detail":"Tobruk port + al-Jufra air base = the logistics bridge sustaining Africa Corps in Mali, Burkina and Niger. Libya is how Russia's Sahel deployments get resupplied."},{"holder":"UAE","channel":"Arms transit","exp":"HIGH","detail":"The northern RSF route; Haftar's financier. Same pattern as Chad — buy a corridor, deny it exists."}],"external":[{"actor":"🇷🇺 Russia","side":"Haftar / LNA","flow":"Africa Corps (ex-Wagner) presence; Feb 2025 Tobruk basing agreement with Belarus; al-Jufra reconstruction; moved SAM-7s and AA systems through Kufra to the RSF","tier":"documented","for":"A Mediterranean+Sahel logistics bridge — the supply line for Africa Corps in Mali/Burkina/Niger"},{"actor":"🇦🇪 UAE","side":"Haftar / LNA + RSF","flow":"Haftar's principal backer; runs the northern RSF arms route through Libyan airspace and al-Kufra","tier":"alleged-credible","for":"Sudanese gold; a client state astride the central Mediterranean"},{"actor":"🇪🇬 Egypt","side":"Haftar (but anti-RSF)","flow":"Backs Haftar politically while pressuring eastern Libya to CLOSE the RSF route — Cairo backs the SAF against the UAE's client","tier":"documented","for":"Border security; Nile/Sudan alignment against the UAE-RSF axis"},{"actor":"🇹🇷 Turkey","side":"GNU (Tripoli)","flow":"Drones and military support that defeated Haftar's 2020 Tripoli offensive; maintains the western balance","tier":"documented","for":"Maritime EEZ claims; a foothold opposite Haftar's patrons"}],"mil":"Libya is not fighting a war so much as hosting one. The state has been split since 2014 between the UN-recognized GNU in Tripoli and Khalifa Haftar's LNA in the east and south, with elections perpetually deferred. The consequential military fact is the corridor: the UAE runs RSF resupply on two air routes, and the northern one lands in Haftar's Libya. Al-Kufra airport in the southeast is the node — IL-76 and AN-26 cargo flights documented by satellite imagery and flight tracking, carrying arms into RSF-held Darfur, including SAM-7s and anti-aircraft systems moved by Wagner. It became the RSF's main supply node after Chad scaled back in 2025, and eastern Libyan authorities briefly closed it on 19 January 2026 under Egyptian diplomatic pressure — which is precisely why the Chad route has become more critical.","pol":"The deeper story is Russia building its Africa bridge. In February 2025 Haftar signed a tripartite agreement with Russia and Belarus on joint use of LNA logistics facilities at Tobruk — an air base and a port — and satellite imagery through April 2026 shows reconstruction at al-Jufra air base. This is the infrastructure that sustains Africa Corps deployments in Mali, Burkina Faso and Niger: Libya is how Russia's Sahel presence gets resupplied. The contradiction is instructive. Moscow has shifted most of its Sudan support from the RSF to the SAF — yet its forces in Libya do not interfere with Haftar's arms flow to the RSF. Flow beats alignment, the same lesson the Myanmar theater teaches.","eco":"Haftar's business is renting geography. He sells transit rights to the UAE, basing to Russia, and sits on much of Libya's oil crescent in a state whose entire economy is hydrocarbons. Egypt backs him politically while simultaneously pressuring him to close the RSF route — because Cairo backs Sudan's army against Abu Dhabi's client. Libya is where three patrons' contradictory interests are all being served by the same man at the same time.","assess":"Libya enters at 67 (ELEVATED, conflict-class), trend up — the other half of a pipeline the board was tracking only half of. The Sudan theater's central scandal is who arms the RSF; the answer runs through two corridors, and until now MERIDIAN mapped Chad and missed Libya. Al-Kufra is the northern gate, and it was the RSF's main node after Chad scaled back. The January 2026 closure under Egyptian pressure proves the corridor can be shut — and that no one has sustained the effort. Layered on top is Russia's Africa bridge: Tobruk basing, al-Jufra reconstruction, and the logistics chain that keeps Africa Corps supplied in Mali, Burkina and Niger. That single fact ties Libya to five other theaters on this board. Watch al-Kufra's status, Russian construction at al-Jufra and Tobruk, whether Egypt sustains the pressure, and any move on the perpetually-deferred elections. Trend estimate — newly entered tracking.","tier":"ELEVATED","domain_tag":"Military","contested":{"summary":"Everyone denies the flights. The satellites keep photographing them.","claims":[{"claim":"Haftar denies taking sides in Sudan's war.","who":"Haftar — and the UAE and Russia, who need the corridor deniable.","evid":"Satellite imagery and flight tracking document IL-76 and AN-26 cargo flights from al-Kufra to RSF-held Sudan (CNN, Libya Observer, Agenzia Nova, repeatedly since 2023). The aircraft types are also Libyan-operated, which is exactly the ambiguity the route is designed to exploit — but the pattern, timing and destination are consistent.","status":"DOCUMENTED-BUT-DENIED"},{"claim":"Russia has shifted its Sudan support to the SAF.","who":"Moscow — the SAF offers a Red Sea naval base the RSF cannot.","evid":"True at the diplomatic level, and simultaneously irrelevant on the ground: Russian forces in Libya do not interfere with Haftar's arms flow to the RSF (Jamestown). Moscow backs the army in Port Sudan while its Libyan client supplies the militia. The alignment changed; the flow did not.","status":"CONTESTED — the policy and the pipeline point different directions"}]},"history":{"roots":"Libya's statelessness has an imperial author before it has a Libyan one. Italy's colonization (1911-43) was genocidal: Omar al-Mukhtar's twenty-year resistance was broken by concentration camps in which a quarter to a third of Cyrenaica's population died — a genocide documented by Libyan historian Ali Abdullatif Ahmida and long erased from European memory. The monarchy Italy's defeat produced was a thin Western client; Gaddafi's 1969 coup answered it with oil-funded personalist rule that deliberately kept institutions hollow so nothing could rival him — 42 years of statelessness-by-design beneath a state's costume. NATO's 2011 intervention decapitated the costume and, as the African Union had warned while proposing the negotiated transition NATO bypassed, left the design: no army, no parties, no institutions — just oil, militias, and geography.","timeline":[{"date":"1969","e":"Gaddafi's coup — 42 years of personalist rule begin."},{"date":"2011","e":"NATO-backed revolution kills Gaddafi; the state collapses."},{"date":"2014","e":"Second civil war; the Tripoli-east split hardens."},{"date":"2019-20","e":"Haftar's Tripoli offensive fails when Turkey intervenes."},{"date":"2020","e":"Ceasefire freezes the split; elections perpetually postponed."},{"date":"2023","e":"Derna dam collapse kills thousands — the hollowed state's price."},{"date":"2025-26","e":"Russia's Africa Corps entrenches east; al-Kufra becomes the RSF arms corridor; four new RSF camps identified (Jul 2026); Egypt/Saudi pressure Haftar over the Russia tilt."},{"date":"Jun 2026","e":"Factions agree another roadmap for long-delayed national elections — the latest in a decade of timetables that have not produced a vote."}],"actors":[{"name":"Khalifa Haftar (LNA)","bio":"The eastern strongman — octogenarian field marshal running a family franchise (sons Saddam and Khaled positioned to inherit); balances Russian patronage against Egyptian and Gulf pressure."},{"name":"Tripoli government (GNU)","bio":"UN-recognized, Turkey-protected, militia-dependent — controls the central bank and oil revenue, not the country."},{"name":"Russia (Africa Corps)","bio":"Eastern Libya as the logistics hub for the whole African project — Sahel supply, RSF arming, Mediterranean presence."},{"name":"UAE / Egypt","bio":"Haftar's original patrons — Abu Dhabi runs RSF supply through his territory; Cairo wants a stable buffer, not a Russian base."}],"bridge":"Every actor in Libya today is farming the hollowness: Haftar's family franchise in the east, militia cartels in Tripoli, Russia's Africa Corps using Cyrenaica — al-Mukhtar's Cyrenaica — as the logistics bridge to the Sahel, and the al-Kufra route arming Sudan's RSF. The migrant-interception economy the EU funds runs through the same detention-camp geography Italy built a century ago, a continuity Ahmida's work makes impossible to unsee. Libya is not a failed state; it is a succeeded design — built hollow twice, by Rome and by Gaddafi, and now rented out by the room. · AND NOW, JUL 2026: another elections roadmap agreed, while Haftar's family enterprise holds the oil crescent and hosts Russia's Sahel logistics hub. Since 2011 every timetable has produced a new arrangement of armed groups rather than a vote.","sources":[{"work":"Genocide in Libya: Shar, a Hidden Colonial History","author":"Ali Abdullatif Ahmida","year":"2020","note":"The Libyan-authored recovery of Italy's concentration-camp genocide in Cyrenaica — the erased foundation."},{"work":"The Making of Modern Libya","author":"Ali Abdullatif Ahmida","year":"1994 (2nd ed. 2009)","note":"State formation, resistance, and the colonial economy from below."},{"work":"A History of Modern Libya","author":"Dirk Vandewalle","year":"2006 (2nd ed. 2012)","note":"The 'hydrocarbon state without institutions' analysis of the monarchy and Gaddafi eras."},{"work":"African Union Ad Hoc Committee on Libya communiqués","author":"African Union","year":"2011","note":"Primary record of the negotiated-transition roadmap NATO's operation bypassed."}]},"rival":{"conf":"HIGH","lens":"A succeeded hollow design — built stateless twice, by Rome and Gaddafi, now rented by the room.","alt":"A simpler two-government-civil-war reading centers the Tripoli-east power struggle without the deeper hollowness thesis.","why":"The power struggle is the surface; the institutional void (why no settlement holds) is the structure. HIGH on the layered read."},"refs":[{"t":"UN Security Council · Panel of Experts on Libya (Mar 2026)","u":"https://www.un.org/securitycouncil/sanctions/1970/panel-of-experts"},{"t":"Arab Center DC · Libya: One Step Forward, Two Steps Back (May 2026)","u":"https://arabcenterdc.org/resource/libya-one-step-forward-two-steps-back/"},{"t":"CFR · Global Conflict Tracker: Libya","u":"https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/civil-war-libya"},{"t":"Democracy Now · headlines (30 Jul 2026)","u":"https://www.democracynow.org/2026/7/30/headlines"},{"t":"Reuters via Foreign Exchanges (Jul 2026)","u":"https://www.foreignexchanges.news/p/world-roundup-july-7-2026"},{"t":"VIF Africa Now, 16-30 Jun 2026","u":"https://www.vifindia.org/2026/july/07/Africa-Now-16-30-june-2026"}],"human":{"dead":5000,"disp":250000,"famine":false,"aid":"militia-mediated","note":"Post-2011 conflict deaths plus the Derna dam collapse (thousands killed, 2023). Separately, the EU-funded interception system holds migrants in detention conditions documented by the UN as inhumane — a human cost the state is paid to produce.","est":true,"basis":"Order-of-magnitude working figure — no single authoritative running count exists for this theater"},"checkmode":"CHECKED","escwhy":"67 = active armed conflict, a recorded human toll, trending UP over the last ten weeks. Composite judgement, not a formula — see the Methodology board for the rubric and its limits.","log":[{"v":"v60","d":"31 Jul 2026","c":"Verified: LNA and GNU-