    `<div class="intro-note" style="margin-bottom:16px">Every state-level source across the platform — statistics offices, official communiqués, UN Security Council listings, ministries. Official data as its own tier alongside the analyst institutions.</div><div class="dx-grid"><div class="dx-box"><div class="dx-t">WHAT EACH KIND OF OFFICIAL SOURCE CAN AND CANNOT ESTABLISH</div><div class="dx-d">Official sources carry authority <b>and</b> interest at the same time. A government’s own figures are simultaneously the most authoritative account available and the most motivated one. That is why they are tiered separately here rather than blended with analyst institutions — not because they are worse, but because they fail differently.</div><div class="dx-d"><b>UN PANEL / GROUP OF EXPERTS</b> — investigative bodies reporting to a Security Council sanctions committee. They gather evidence and name actors, and their findings are frequently the best documentation that exists. <b>They do not adjudicate.</b> A panel finding is not a verdict, and states routinely reject them without any legal consequence.</div><div class="dx-d"><b>GENOCIDE DETERMINATION</b> — when a foreign ministry or state department declares that genocide is occurring, that is an <b>executive branch designation</b>, not a court finding. It carries real policy consequences and real evidentiary work behind it, but <b>it is not a judicial verdict and does not require one.</b> Only a court — the ICJ between states, the ICC against individuals — can rule on the legal question, and those cases take years. Conflating the two is the most common error made with this board’s Sudan entries.</div><div class="dx-d"><b>ICC WARRANT vs CONVICTION</b> — a warrant means a pre-trial chamber found <i>reasonable grounds to believe</i> a person committed the crime. It is a threshold for arrest, <b>not a finding of guilt.</b> Most warrants on this board have never been executed, because the ICC has no police force and depends on member states making arrests they often decline to make.</div><div class="dx-d"><b>COMMISSIONS OF INQUIRY and OHCHR reporting</b> — fact-finding mandates that document violations and recommend action. Authoritative on what happened, without power to compel anything about it.</div><div class="dx-d"><b>NATIONAL STATISTICS OFFICES</b> — the only source for most economic data, and produced by the government the data describes. Direction of travel is usually more reliable than level. Where this board carries an official figure that outside estimates dispute, the theater record says so.</div></div></div>`+
