 {t:'venezuela',ind:'Aug 1 dialogue convenes — or collapses',mean:'If the Rodríguez-Figuera working group actually meets, the managed transition is real; if it collapses or Machado’s bloc breaks it, the US “strategic patience” plan loses its vehicle.',hz:'1 Aug 2026',due:'1 Aug 2026',st:'NEAR',verdict:'PREMISE CHANGED \u2014 CLOSED ON ITS DUE DATE, 1 AUG 2026: this wire asked whether an Aug 1 dialogue between the Rodr\u00edguez-Figuera working group and Machado\'s bloc would convene or collapse. The date has arrived and the question is void: MADURO WAS SEIZED IN A US RAID IN JANUARY, Delcy Rodr\u00edguez\'s 180-day interim mandate has since EXPIRED WITH NO AGREED SUCCESSION, and the country absorbed twin earthquakes in June that killed roughly 3,000 and caused \u002437bn in damage. The wire was watching whether negotiation could avert intervention; the intervention answered it seven months ago. CLOSED WITHOUT A VERDICT ON ITS OWN TERMS \u2014 recorded rather than deleted, because a wire set on the wrong question is a scoring failure worth keeping visible.'},
