      +'<b>THE ESCALATION LAYER.</b> '+DB.filter(function(d){return d.escalation}).length+' conflicts carry a trajectory read: the rung they sit on, the direction they are moving, what pushes them up, and what could bend them down. Each is tagged with the analytical frameworks that actually explain it \u2014 Kahn\u2019s ladder, the conflict curve, the security dilemma, Zartman\u2019s ripeness, proxy dynamics, the political economy of war, the ethnic security dilemma, deterrence, and the Thucydides Trap. <b>Every framework is given its limits alongside its predictions</b>, and no conflict is tagged with only one, because no single lens explains a war.<br><br>'
